-- title:
--   Integrality at both prolongations of K-integral functions on X₀(Nq)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a level $N\ge 1$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$; fix moreover `data`, consisting of a monic polynomial $\Phi$ over $\mathbb Z[X]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ with $\Phi(j,j_q)=0$, together with `hKr`, the Kronecker congruence asserting that the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ equals $(X^q-Y)(X-Y^q)$ in bivariate form, and the hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ that the two degeneracy embeddings `heckeAlphaBar`, `heckeBetaBar` of level $N$, $q$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ are integral ring homomorphisms. Let $P$ be a place specialisation of these data and $R$ a prolongation tuple over $P$, and assume $q\nmid N$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and let $t$ lie in `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $Nq$ inside Laurent series, and assume that the Laurent series of $t$ lies in `jIntegralClosure (N * q) A K`, i.e. lies in `fieldOver (N * q) K` and is integral over the ring `jRing A K`. Then three assertions hold. First, $t$ belongs to the integers `R.R₁.integers` of the first prolongation, and its first residue `R.residue₁`, viewed in the characteristic-$q$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldC k N` (the subfield of $k$-Laurent series generated by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k N`), is integral over the $k$-subalgebra generated by `jGeomGen k N`. Second, the same holds for the second prolongation, its integers `R.R₂.integers` and its residue `R.residue₂`. Third, for every place $v$ of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` over $k$ whose valuation subring contains `jGeomGen k N`, and every place $V$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `P.reduceFst V = v` — that is, $P.\mathrm{sp}$ applied to the restriction of $V$ along the first degeneracy embedding is $v$ — there is $a\in A$ with `V.HasValue t a`: $t$ lies in the valuation subring of $V$ and its residue there is the image of $a$.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the normalisation of the $j$-line in $K(j,j_{Nq})$ and the two components of the special fibre at $q$: a function integral over $A[j]$ is integral for both Gauss prolongations, with residues integral over $k[\bar\jmath]$, and takes values in $A$ at all places lying over places of the fibre where $\bar\jmath$ is regular. It supports the comparisons of the two residue maps and the criteria for vanishing of values used in the node-descent analysis of $X_0(Nq)$ in characteristic $q$.
